    "title": "New Philadelphia Man Rams Cruiser After 26-Minute, 100-MPH Chase - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sofia Aragon ,\n10 hours ago\nA traffic stop near South Broadway and the U.S. Route 250 eastbound exit in New Philadelphia exploded into a 26-minute pursuit Tuesday evening, with speeds topping 100 mph before officers boxed in the fleeing driver on Interstate 77 and arrested him. New Philadelphia Police Chief Tessa Pohovey said the chase ended around 7:09 p.m., about one mile south of the Stone Creek exit, after the driver allegedly rammed a police cruiser during the maneuver that finally stopped him.\nRead full article\nAdd to Preferred Sources",
